      "summary": "After Ahab's death Moab rebels, and in Samaria his son King Ahaziah falls through the lattice of his upper chamber and lies badly injured. Instead of turning to the Lord, he sends messengers to ask Baal-zebub, the god of Ekron, whether he will recover. The angel of the Lord sends Elijah to intercept them with a stinging question — is there not a God in Israel? — and a verdict: the king will not come down from his bed but will surely die. When the messengers describe 'an hairy man, girt with a girdle of leather,' Ahaziah knows at once it is Elijah the Tishbite. He sends a captain with fifty soldiers to seize the prophet on his hilltop, and fire from heaven consumes them; a second captain and fifty meet the same end. The third captain falls on his knees and begs for his life, and the angel tells Elijah to go down with him unafraid. Elijah delivers the sentence to the king's face, Ahaziah dies as the word of the Lord said, and because he has no son his brother Jehoram takes the throne.",
