      "summary": "In Jehoiakim's days Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon comes up, and Jehoiakim serves him three years, then rebels. The Lord sends raiding bands of Chaldeans, Syrians, Moabites, and Ammonites against Judah 'to destroy it,' as He had spoken by His prophets — surely at His commandment, for the sins of Manasseh and for the innocent blood that the Lord would not pardon. The king of Egypt comes no more out of his land, because Babylon has taken everything from the river of Egypt to the Euphrates. Jehoiakim dies, and his eighteen-year-old son Jehoiachin reigns only three months before Nebuchadnezzar's servants besiege Jerusalem. Jehoiachin goes out to the king of Babylon with his mother, his servants, his princes, and his officers, and is carried away captive in Nebuchadnezzar's eighth year. Nebuchadnezzar strips the treasures of the temple and the palace, cuts in pieces the golden vessels Solomon had made, and deports ten thousand captives — princes, mighty men, craftsmen, and smiths — leaving only the poorest sort of the people of the land. He makes Jehoiachin's uncle Mattaniah king and changes his name to Zedekiah, who reigns eleven years and does evil — and then rebels against the king of Babylon.",
